25. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

Security is a core product requirement.

Implement:

Authentication:

* Secure authentication.
* Secure session handling.
* Password reset protection.
* Email verification where configured.

Authorization:

* Verify ownership of every user-specific record.
* Enforce least privilege.
* Use PostgreSQL RLS.
* Validate permissions server-side.

Input validation:

* Validate all incoming data.
* Use Zod schemas.
* Sanitize user-generated rich text.
* Prevent stored XSS.

Web security:

* Protect against CSRF where applicable.
* Prevent SQL injection through parameterized queries and safe ORM/database access.
* Apply rate limiting to sensitive endpoints.
* Use secure HTTP headers.
* Apply a suitable Content Security Policy.
* Protect against IDOR.
* Avoid leaking sensitive errors.

Secrets:

* Keep credentials in environment variables.
* Never expose Supabase service-role keys in client code.
* Never commit .env files.
* Provide a .env.example without real credentials.

File uploads:

* Restrict file types and sizes.
* Validate actual file content where possible.
* Use private storage.
* Generate secure access links.
* Prevent unauthorized file access.

Privacy:

* Keep journal entries private.
* Minimize personal data collection.
* Provide account deletion and data export mechanisms.

