32. IMPORTANT IMPLEMENTATION RULES

These rules are mandatory.

1. Do not build a static mockup and call it a completed application.
2. Do not create buttons that have no functionality.
3. Do not use fake charts or hardcoded productivity statistics in the real application.
4. Do not use placeholder links for supposedly working features.
5. Every implemented form must validate and save real data.
6. Every user-specific page must load the authenticated user’s actual data.
7. Every destructive action must require appropriate confirmation.
8. Every page must have loading, error, empty, and success states where appropriate.
9. Do not expose API keys or sensitive information.
10. Do not overcomplicate the initial implementation.
11. Prioritize a stable, working MVP before adding optional features.
12. Do not silently ignore errors.
13. Do not claim that an integration, test, deployment, or security feature works unless it has been verified.
14. Keep the interface consistent with the official brand palette.
15. Maintain clean, readable, maintainable TypeScript.
16. Make the application usable without any paid third-party service beyond what is explicitly configured.
17. Do not add unnecessary gamification, leaderboards, social feeds, or distracting features.
18. Never sacrifice user privacy for analytics or personalization.

